{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1524170-homebrews-of-the-second-circle","id":1524170,"title":"Homebrews of the Second Circle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-16T19:33:56-07:00","id":1524170,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Homebrews of the Second Circle?","content":"Similar to the excellent <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\">Homebrews of the First Circle Thread</a>, I thought this would be an opportunity to share either via post or link examples of 2nd Circle Demons. Stats are ideal, but not necessary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 10-16-2023, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T20:28:57-07:00","id":1524175,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://exalted-13.obsidianportal.com/characters/fel-garen-the-shining-rule\" target=\"_blank\">Fel Garen, the Shining Rule | Exalted: The Legend of Denandsor | Obsidian Portal</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Fel Garen, the Shining Rule</b><ul><li><a href=\"https://exalted-13.obsidianportal.com/search?tag=Demon\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://exalted-13.obsidianportal.com/search?tag=Denandsor\" target=\"_blank\">Denandsor</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://exalted-13.obsidianportal.com/search?tag=Second+Circle\" target=\"_blank\">Second Circle</a></li> </ul><br /> <i>A powerful Second Circle demon trapped in Denandsor.</i> <b>Description:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Species: Demon (Second Circle)<br /> Profession: Bound Demon<br /> <br /> Fel Garen appears as a floating school of electric blue geometric shapes, lazily swirling around one another not unlike a mobile. When agitated or pleased, the shapes swirl faster. He has no analogue to a \u201chead\u201d, and when he speaks the voice simply emerges from the air somewhere near him. <b>Bio:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Fel Garen was during the waning years of old Denandsor\u2019s existence, bound in place to protect and keep safe a sorcerer\u2019s library. Fel Garen claims to not remember much of these days, as it was a very long time ago and his memory simply does not retain everything, particularly as it pertains to humans. Every since then, he\u2019s been forced to maintain his long and lonely vigil. In that time, he read the entire library several times over out of sheer idleness, and simply waited to be released from his task.<br /> <br /> He was re-discovered by the Archaeological Society when the refugees of Great Forks arrived to resettle the city. When the scavenger lords breached the sanctum of his library, Fel Garen reacted much the way he was expected to- by slaughtering the puny humans who dared enter into his domain. As a tense standoff ensued, however, Fel Garen was given pause- considering that his orders were to <i>protect</i> and <i>keep safe</i> the library, would not these curious humans be able to access the library provided they did not damage or remove any of the books? <a href=\"https://exalted-13.obsidianportal.com/characters/diamond-azure\" target=\"_blank\">Diamond Azure</a> agreed to his offer, and the deal was set- the Archaological Society could study and copy the books in the library as they pleased, provided they did not remove or damage anything.<br /> Fel Garen did not remain pleased with this situation for long, but not because of any infraction on the part of his now comrades. Rather, he overheard from scholars who were visiting the library that Denandsor was a city without slaves. Fel Garen realized that he could try for true freedom- something he thought would be impossible to realize without returning to Malfeas. So he begged for a moment of Diamond Azure\u2019s time and made his pitch: if Denandsor truly did not hold to slavery, so too must he be set free.<br /> <br /> After some consideration, the Circle chose to free Fel Garen provided he abides by the conditions offered to all slaves freed by the city of Denandsor- that he provide two years of indentured service to the city. Fel Garen agree to this condition just in time to be deployed against <a href=\"https://exalted-13.obsidianportal.com/characters/ma-ha-suchi\" target=\"_blank\">Ma Ha Suchi</a>\u2018s army during the Battle of Denandsor. Fel Garen fought well, acting as something of a mobile anti-infantry weapon, and he was wounded quite badly twice over the course of the two-day battle.<br /> <br /> Since the Battle of Denandsor, Fel Garen was able to rest on his laurels- in the absence of massive battles, there simply isn\u2019t enough call for his unique abilities. Following the end of his two years of service, Fel Garen opened a bookstore. Now that Fel Garen is free, he seeks to be the one who controls the books rather than the other way around.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T19:12:21-07:00","id":1524210,"title":"","content":"From <a href=\"http://Alean,%20the%20Scholar%20Lovelorn%20Demon%20of%20the%20Second%20Circle%20Indulgent%20Soul%20of%20the%20House%20of%20the%20Scorpion%20%20This%20is%20a%20lesser%20age,%20fallen%20far%20from%20what%20was%20before,%20and%20what%20greatness%20can%20yet%20be%20found%20arises%20only%20where%20some%20glimmer%20of%20that%20ancient%20light%20remains.%20Such%20is%20the%20proclamation%20of%20Alean,%20the%20Scholar%20Lovelorn,%20whose%20heart%20beats%20eternally%20for%20a%20woman%20two%20thousand%20years%20in%20her%20grave.%20It%20is%20said%20that%20when%20her%20oversoul%20fell%20in%20love%20with%20that%20golden%20lady,%20his%20Indulgent%20soul%20died%20of%20that%20passion,%20and%20from%20it%20was%20born%20the%20Scholar.%20%20In%20seeming,%20Alean%20is%20a%20short%20and%20compact%20woman%20who%20wears%20her%20ink-black%20hair%20in%20an%20archaic%20bun,%20pierced%20by%20needles%20of%20gold.%20Her%20eyes%20are%20the%20eyes%20of%20a%20newt,%20and%20amphibians%20of%20all%20kinds%20love%20her%20and%20sing%20ancient%20laments%20for%20her%20and%20her%20beloved%20in%20the%20evening%20and%20the%20night.%20She%20dresses%20modestly,%20and%20some%20say%20this%20is%20due%20to%20her%20wish%20to%20keep%20herself%20chaste%20for%20her%20long-lost%20love%20-%20but%20this%20is%20not%20so.%20Rather,%20it%20is%20because%20she%20long%20ago%20suffered%20many%20wounds%20as%20stigmata%20during%20the%20Usurpation,%20and%20beneath%20her%20robes%20she%20is%20wrapped%20from%20neck%20to%20toe%20in%20enchanted%20bandages%20which%20seal%20her%20toxic%20blood%20within,%20and%20cover%20the%20cavity%20which%20gapes%20above%20her%20heart.%20%20In%20manner,%20the%20Scholar%20is%20a%20strict%20disciplinarian,%20though%20she%20knows%20the%20object%20of%20her%20affections%20would%20not%20love%20her%20for%20this.%20She%20has%20lived%20many%20mortal%20lifetimes%20of%20despair,%20and%20this%20discipline%20has%20been%20the%20result;%20if%20she%20had%20not%20assumed%20it,%20she%20would%20have%20slain%20herself%20long%20ago.%20The%20order%20she%20imposed%20upon%20herself%20became%20habit,%20and%20now%20it%20has%20become%20her%20general%20manner%20in%20dealing%20with%20the%20students%20of%20her%20oversoul,%20as%20she%20often%20does%20-%20she%20is%20one%20of%20his%20favoured%20professors,%20and%20is%20deeply%20learned%20in%20the%20esoterica%20of%20cosmology,%20abstract%20sorcery%20and%20the%20Essence-sciences%20of%20the%20High%20First%20Age.%20%20Summoning%20(Obscurity%204/5):%20Alean%20is%20summoned%20by%20sorcerers%20to%20instruct%20them%20in%20the%20intricacies%20of%20strange%20and%20abstract%20spells,%20to%20identify%20the%20purposes%20and%20function%20of%20ancient%20Artefacts,%20and%20to%20perform%20subtle%20workings%20of%20power.%20She%20is%20a%20sorceress%20of%20the%20Celestial%20Circle,%20but%20her%20preferred%20spells%20are%20rarely%20overt%20in%20action,%20and%20often%20seem%20underwhelming%20for%20her%20power%20and%20knowledge.%20Nevertheless,%20a%20prospective%20student%20would%20be%20well-advised%20to%20be%20cautious%20-%20to%20the%20Scholar%20Lovelorn,%20sorcery%20is%20not%20a%20tool%20for%20advancement%20or%20material%20gain,%20but%20a%20sacrament%20to%20her%20love,%20and%20demanding%20that%20she%20perform%20or%20teach%20her%20lore%20for%20such%20profane%20reasons%20causes%20her%20to%20gain%20Limit.%20In%20the%20extremities%20of%20rage%20she%20sheds%20her%20human%20appearance%20and%20becomes%20a%20terrible%20beast%20of%20amphibian%20aspect%20to%20destroy%20those%20who%20would%20profane%20her%20lore.%20%20Though%20she%20has%20no%20children%20of%20her%20body,%20many%20are%20those%20of%20her%20adoption.%20Alean%20may%20escape%20from%20Hell%20through%20the%20Salinan%20Working,%20when%20a%20child%20of%20high%20birth%20but%20low%20circumstances%20begs%20the%20night%20for%20tutelage%20in%20arts%20beyond%20their%20ken.%20Then%20she%20emerges%20and%20takes%20the%20child%20away,%20raising%20them%20herself%20and%20instructing%20them%20as%20her%20child%20and%20apprentice,%20before%20sending%20them%20out%20into%20the%20world%20again%20to%20do%20as%20they%20will.%20It%20is%20said%20that%20she%20holds%20some%20alliance%20with%20the%20ancient%20Lunar%20called%20the%20Wolf%20at%20the%20Door,%20who%20sometimes%20seeks%20to%20arrange%20such%20releases%20for%20her,%20and%20may%20often%20use%20her%20children%20in%20his%20own%20plots%20thereafter.%20%20Buha,%20the%20President%20of%20Owls%20Demon%20of%20the%20Second%20Circle%20Messenger%20Soul%20of%20the%20House%20of%20the%20Scorpion%20%20Two%20hundred%20and%20sixteen%20number%20the%20eyes%20of%20Buha,%20whose%20many%20bodies%20flit%20across%20moonless%20skies.%20Demonomicae%20say%20they%20are%20kin%20in%20some%20way%20to%20the%20decanthrope,%20for%20their%20multiplicity,%20or%20even%20that%20Dascal%20shaped%20them%20from%20a%20demon%20of%20that%20breed%20(and%20such%20a%20thing%20would%20be%20to%20the%20liking%20of%20the%20House%20of%20the%20Scorpion,%20as%20high%20heresy%20against%20the%20Descending%20Hierarchy)%20but%20if%20this%20is%20true,%20neither%20the%20President%20nor%20the%20House%20will%20speak%20of%20it.%20%20By%20nature%20and%20profession,%20Buha%20is%20a%20herald%20and%20and%20augur,%20for%20which%20skill%20they%20are%20sometimes%20named%20the%20Night-Seer.%20Their%20stock-in-trade%20is%20omens,%20both%20in%20their%20spreading%20and%20their%20reading.%20For%20the%20latter,%20they%20have%20learned%20countless%20divinatory%20arts%20across%20their%20long%20centuries,%20and%20with%20their%20hundred-and-eight%20bodies,%20each%20some%20creature%20of%20the%20night,%20they%20sit%20in%20council%20and%20debate%20signs%20and%20portents%20to%20a%20nicety,%20giving%20readings%20of%20the%20past%20and%20present%20of%20uncanny%20accuracy%20-%20though%20they%20often%20ask%20esoteric%20prices%20for%20such%20prognostication,%20the%20true%20worth%20of%20which%20becomes%20clear%20only%20later.%20%20If%20soothsayers%20are%20ten-a-street%20in%20most%20cities,%20however,%20omen-heralds%20are%20a%20rarer%20trade%20-%20but%20one%20in%20which%20the%20President%20excels.%20Partly,%20this%20is%20due%20to%20their%20magic.%20They%20know%20songs%20which,%20when%20sung%20by%20night,%20make%20rain%20fall%20red%20and%20causes%20beasts%20to%20bear%20two-headed%20offspring,%20and%20dances%20on%20the%20wing%20which,%20when%20danced%20in%20the%20evening,%20bring%20omens%20of%20good%20fortune%20and%20prosperity.%20But%20it%20is%20also%20partly%20due%20to%20their%20expertise%20in%20simple%20trickery.%20They%20can%20mimic%20voices%20with%20perfection,%20can%20burrow%20into%20the%20hearts%20of%20men%20and%20demons%20and%20use%20their%20bodies%20to%20spread%20rumours%20and%20deceit,%20and%20know%20well%20how%20to%20stir%20fear,%20resentment,%20panic%20and%20righteousness.%20All%20these%20services%20they%20will%20perform%20-%20for%20the%20right%20price.%20%20Summoning%20(Obscurity%202/4):%20Sorcerers%20call%20the%20President%20of%20Owls%20to%20interpret%20signs%20and%20omens%20for%20them,%20to%20carry%20messages%20between%20far-distant%20parts%20of%20their%20domains%20-%20for%20what%20one%20body%20knows,%20all%20know%20-%20to%20act%20as%20familiars%20to%20whisper%20of%20them%20of%20what%20their%20people%20do,%20and%20to%20manipulate%20populations%20to%20their%20will.%20Often,%20Buha%20has%20been%20called%20to%20incite%20hatred%20of%20a%20people%E2%80%99s%20lords%20before%20a%20sorcerer%20comes%20a-conquering,%20or%20to%20act%20as%20a%20signaller%20ahead%20of%20invasion%20to%20hidden%20elements%20of%20rebellion.%20These%20things%20they%20do%20without%20complaint,%20so%20long%20as%20their%20price%20is%20right,%20for%20their%20mentality%20is%20mercenary.%20In%20payment,%20they%20ask%20all%20manner%20of%20things%20-%20that%20the%20name%20of%20a%20firstborn%20child%20be%20this%20rather%20than%20that,%20favours%20to%20be%20named%20in%20future,%20or%20that%20they%20be%20given%20the%20pick%20of%20three%20men%20from%20a%20sorcerer%E2%80%99s%20holdings%20to%20go%20with%20them,%20wherever%20they%20take%20them.%20%20Often,%20these%20prices%20seem%20little%20enough%20to%20such%20great%20men%20at%20first,%20but%20many%20years%20later%20have%20unforeseen%20effects.%20Sacrifices%20long-presumed%20dead%20will%20return%20with%20new%20and%20dark%20learning%20to%20challenge%20their%20former%20masters,%20demon-chosen%20names%20will%20incite%20the%20hatred%20of%20those%20who%20might%20have%20been%20allies,%20and%20favours%20that%20seemed%20light%20at%20first%20become%20chains%20later%20on.%20Some%20perceive%20a%20deeper%20meaning%20in%20these%20turns%20of%20chance%20than%20the%20disasters%20and%20calamities%20loved%20by%20the%20children%20of%20the%20Ultimate%20Darkness,%20and%20even%20whisper%20that%20Buha%20has%20a%20standing%20arrangement%20with%20the%20viziers%20of%20Fate,%20acting%20to%20further%20the%20plans%20of%20destiny%20in%20some%20hidden%20way.%20But%20what%20agents%20of%20Heaven%20would%20consort%20with%20such%20a%20blood-drinking%20creature%20of%20night?%20Such%20is%20always%20a%20part%20of%20the%20President%E2%80%99s%20retainer.%20%20Buha%20may%20slip%20the%20bonds%20of%20Hell%20when%20an%20owl%20or%20other%20night-bird%20drinks%20the%20blood%20of%20a%20young%20man%20and%20a%20suckling%20lamb%20in%20a%20single%20night;%20that%20bird%20becomes%20one%20of%20their%20many%20bodies,%20and%20flies%20out%20to%20bring%20more%20through%20to%20Creation.%20They%20gain%20Limit%20when%20their%20prices%20are%20denied%20or%20cheated%20after%20having%20been%20promised,%20and%20will%20exact%20terrible%20revenges%20upon%20such%20as%20do%20so%20-%20though%20they%20may%20be%20long%20in%20coming.%20%20Tanlato,%20the%20Inquisitor%20Circumspect%20Demon%20of%20the%20Second%20Circle%20Warden%20Soul%20of%20the%20House%20of%20the%20Scorpion%20%20Two%20heads%20has%20Tanlato,%20the%20Heron%20Who%20Eats%20Dreams.%20That%20is%20a%20name%20he%20buries%20deep,%20though,%20and%20there%20are%20few%20who%20know%20it.%20He%20has%20two%20forms%20as%20well.%20One%20is%20a%20man%20of%20saturnine%20aspect,%20tall%20and%20dark-haired,%20with%20the%20severely-carven%20features%20of%20a%20man%20of%20the%20Blessed%20Isle%20and%20the%20blood%20of%20Danada,%20but%20with%20doubled%20pupils%20in%20each%20eye%20and%20teeth%20of%20hard%20metal.%20The%20other%20is%20a%20two-headed%20heron%20whose%20height%20can%20vary%20from%20reaching%20a%20tall%20man%E2%80%99s%20knee%20to%20towering%20several%20feet%20above%20him,%20and%20whose%20beaks%20are%20made%20of%20steel.%20In%20either%20form%20he%20goes%20clad%20in%20black%20and%20red,%20whether%20these%20be%20his%20feathers%20or%20his%20robes,%20and%20he%20may%20be%20known%20by%20the%20clack%20of%20his%20talons%20upon%20the%20earth.%20%20In%20demeanour%20the%20Inquisitor%20Circumspect%20is%20reserved%20but%20keen%20of%20wit,%20rarely%20failing%20to%20offer%20a%20cutting%20remark%20when%20he%20perceives%20some%20failing%20he%20can%20criticise%20-%20and%20he%20sees%20many,%20for%20his%20eyes%20are%20just%20as%20keen.%20Often%20he%20resides%20within%20his%20greater%20self,%20acting%20to%20police%20and%20regulate%20the%20many%20students%20of%20Dascal%20-%20but%20he%20may%20also%20go%20abroad,%20leaving%20his%20demons%20to%20do%20so%20in%20his%20stead.%20For%20this%20he%20is%20little-loved%20by%20those%20students,%20but%20it%20has%20long%20since%20taught%20him%20how%20to%20keep%20order%20even%20amongst%20the%20rowdiest%20and%20most%20unmanageable%20populations,%20and%20has%20become%20a%20masterful%20driver%20of%20slaves%20and%20servants%20of%20all%20kinds.%20His%20eyes%20can%20perceive%20hatred%20and%20resentment%20as%20easily%20as%20another%20might%20note%20the%20colour%20of%20a%20man%E2%80%99s%20hair,%20and%20with%20attention%20and%20time%20can%20discern%20particulars%20such%20as%20against%20whom%20that%20resentment%20is%20directed.%20%20His%20most%20significant%20ability,%20though,%20is%20known%20to%20few%20-%20and%20Tanlato%20puts%20great%20effort%20to%20keeping%20it%20this%20way.%20His%20beaks%20have%20the%20power%20to%20plunge%20into%20the%20head%20of%20another,%20and%20there%20his%20sensitive%20tongues%20can%20taste%20the%20memories%20of%20his%20victims.%20With%20the%20right%20head%20he%20picks%20out%20memories%20of%20events%20and%20places,%20and%20with%20the%20left%20he%20devours%20abstract%20knowledge.%20Thus%20it%20is%20that%20few%20students%20go%20forth%20from%20the%20House%20of%20the%20Scorpion%20with%20any%20knowledge%20of%20where%20to%20find%20it%20again,%20and%20Dascal%20is%20protected%20from%20the%20dangers%20of%20his%20great%20vice.%20The%20Inquisitor%20has%20served%20this%20office%20since%20his%20creation,%20but%20some%20say%20that%20he%20has%20become%20bitter%20with%20the%20years,%20and%20does%20so%20now%20out%20of%20a%20sense%20of%20obligation,%20habit%20and%20the%20fear%20of%20what%20might%20befall%20his%20oversoul%20-%20and%20thus%20himself%20-%20were%20the%20House%20left%20without%20his%20guardianship.%20%20Summoning%20(Obscurity%203/6):%20Demonologists%20summon%20the%20Inquisitor%20Circumspect%20to%20put%20down%20rebellions%20and%20command%20unruly%20servants,%20to%20pick%20out%20spies%20and%20rebels%20amongst%20their%20followers,%20and%20for%20his%20knowledge%20and%20might%20as%20a%20sorcerer.%20In%20this%20he%20is%20as%20practical%20as%20his%20sister%20Alean%20is%20abstract,%20and%20knows%20many%20spells%20for%20confinement,%20death%20and%20the%20warding-away%20of%20hostile%20powers%20and%20attention.%20Those%20who%20know%20of%20Tanlato%E2%80%99s%20other%20talent,%20however,%20summon%20him%20to%20be%20a%20censor%20and%20interrogator,%20for%20in%20the%20taste%20of%20the%20memories%20he%20swallows%20he%20can%20glean%20much%20from%20victims%E2%80%99%20minds%20-%20and%20what%20he%20cannot%20take%20by%20magic,%20he%20can%20take%20by%20torment,%20as%20he%20has%20had%20long%20practice%20in%20the%20art%20of%20interrogation.%20%20Furthermore,%20he%20is%20a%20master%20of%20the%20Black%20Heron%20Style,%20a%20discipline%20of%20his%20own%20invention%20and%20an%20offshoot%20of%20Crane%20Style.%20This%20Style%20focuses%20on%20non-fatal%20defence%20and%20subduing%20attacks%20in%20a%20manner%20similar%20to%20its%20origin,%20but%20where%20Crane%20Style%20relies%20upon%20enlightened%20discourse%20to%20educate%20and%20edify%20its%20target,%20the%20Black%20Heron%20Style%20instead%20uses%20a%20combination%20of%20force%20and%20humiliation%20to%20subdue%20the%20target%20to%20its%20practitioner%E2%80%99s%20will%20through%20fear%20and%20coercion.%20Although%20known%20in%20Creation,%20it%20is%20poorly-regarded%20as%20unsportsmanlike%20and%20reviled%20as%20a%20dark%20mirror%20of%20the%20Crane.%20%20Some%20say%20the%20Inquisitor%E2%80%99s%20role%20as%20a%20censor%20has%20brought%20him%20into%20some%20alignment%20with%20the%20End%20of%20All%20Wisdom,%20the%20ancient%20enemy%20of%20Dascal,%20and%20that%20he%20has%20some%20plot%20to%20muzzle,%20or%20perhaps%20somehow%20even%20overthrow%20and%20replace%20his%20greater%20self%20in%20the%20ranks%20of%20the%20Unquestionable.%20If%20such%20a%20thing%20is%20possible,%20perhaps%20Dascal%20would%20marvel%20at%20the%20beauty%20of%20his%20own%20destruction%20in%20the%20moment%20of%20betrayal.%20Tanlato%20gains%20Limit%20when%20one%20he%20had%20thought%20broken%20defies%20him,%20and%20may%20escape%20into%20Creation%20when%20the%20head%20of%20a%20monastery%20or%20formal%20school%20is%20imprisoned%20by%20rebellious%20students%20and%20begs%20for%20anyone%20to%20deliver%20him%20and%20restore%20the%20right%20order%20of%20the%20world.%20Then%20the%20Inquisitor%20will%20appear%20and%20with%20hands%20and%20beaks%20and%20sorcery%20set%20things%20to%20rights%20for%20that%20school,%20before%20departing%20on%20errands%20of%20his%20own%20-%20but%20who%20can%20tell,%20after%20he%20has%20come,%20whether%20all%20is%20as%20it%20once%20was%20or%20what%20he%20has%20taken?\" target=\"_blank\">Sufficient Velocity</a>, we have three 2E 2nd circle demon fluff write ups:<br /> <br /> <b>Alean, the Scholar Lovelorn</b><br /> <i>Demon of the Second Circle<br /> Indulgent Soul of the House of the Scorpion</i><br /> <br /> This is a lesser age, fallen far from what was before, and what greatness can yet be found arises only where some glimmer of that ancient light remains. Such is the proclamation of Alean, the Scholar Lovelorn, whose heart beats eternally for a woman two thousand years in her grave. It is said that when her oversoul fell in love with that golden lady, his Indulgent soul died of that passion, and from it was born the Scholar.<br /> <br /> In seeming, Alean is a short and compact woman who wears her ink-black hair in an archaic bun, pierced by needles of gold. Her eyes are the eyes of a newt, and amphibians of all kinds love her and sing ancient laments for her and her beloved in the evening and the night. She dresses modestly, and some say this is due to her wish to keep herself chaste for her long-lost love - but this is not so. Rather, it is because she long ago suffered many wounds as stigmata during the Usurpation, and beneath her robes she is wrapped from neck to toe in enchanted bandages which seal her toxic blood within, and cover the cavity which gapes above her heart.<br /> <br /> In manner, the Scholar is a strict disciplinarian, though she knows the object of her affections would not love her for this. She has lived many mortal lifetimes of despair, and this discipline has been the result; if she had not assumed it, she would have slain herself long ago. The order she imposed upon herself became habit, and now it has become her general manner in dealing with the students of her oversoul, as she often does - she is one of his favoured professors, and is deeply learned in the esoterica of cosmology, abstract sorcery and the Essence-sciences of the High First Age.<br /> <br /> <i>Summoning (Obscurity 4/5): </i>Alean is summoned by sorcerers to instruct them in the intricacies of strange and abstract spells, to identify the purposes and function of ancient Artefacts, and to perform subtle workings of power. She is a sorceress of the Celestial Circle, but her preferred spells are rarely overt in action, and often seem underwhelming for her power and knowledge. Nevertheless, a prospective student would be well-advised to be cautious - to the Scholar Lovelorn, sorcery is not a tool for advancement or material gain, but a sacrament to her love, and demanding that she perform or teach her lore for such profane reasons causes her to gain Limit. In the extremities of rage she sheds her human appearance and becomes a terrible beast of amphibian aspect to destroy those who would profane her lore.<br /> <br /> Though she has no children of her body, many are those of her adoption. Alean may escape from Hell through the Salinan Working, when a child of high birth but low circumstances begs the night for tutelage in arts beyond their ken. Then she emerges and takes the child away, raising them herself and instructing them as her child and apprentice, before sending them out into the world again to do as they will. It is said that she holds some alliance with the ancient Lunar called the Wolf at the Door, who sometimes seeks to arrange such releases for her, and may often use her children in his own plots thereafter.<br /> <br /> <b>Buha, the President of Owls</b><br /> <i>Demon of the Second Circle<br /> Messenger Soul of the House of the Scorpion</i><br /> <br /> Two hundred and sixteen number the eyes of Buha, whose many bodies flit across moonless skies. Demonomicae say they are kin in some way to the decanthrope, for their multiplicity, or even that Dascal shaped them from a demon of that breed (and such a thing would be to the liking of the House of the Scorpion, as high heresy against the Descending Hierarchy) but if this is true, neither the President nor the House will speak of it.<br /> <br /> By nature and profession, Buha is a herald and and augur, for which skill they are sometimes named the Night-Seer. Their stock-in-trade is omens, both in their spreading and their reading. For the latter, they have learned countless divinatory arts across their long centuries, and with their hundred-and-eight bodies, each some creature of the night, they sit in council and debate signs and portents to a nicety, giving readings of the past and present of uncanny accuracy - though they often ask esoteric prices for such prognostication, the true worth of which becomes clear only later.<br /> <br /> If soothsayers are ten-a-street in most cities, however, omen-heralds are a rarer trade - but one in which the President excels. Partly, this is due to their magic. They know songs which, when sung by night, make rain fall red and causes beasts to bear two-headed offspring, and dances on the wing which, when danced in the evening, bring omens of good fortune and prosperity. But it is also partly due to their expertise in simple trickery. They can mimic voices with perfection, can burrow into the hearts of men and demons and use their bodies to spread rumours and deceit, and know well how to stir fear, resentment, panic and righteousness. All these services they will perform - for the right price.<br /> <br /> <i>Summoning (Obscurity 2/4):</i> Sorcerers call the President of Owls to interpret signs and omens for them, to carry messages between far-distant parts of their domains - for what one body knows, all know - to act as familiars to whisper of them of what their people do, and to manipulate populations to their will. Often, Buha has been called to incite hatred of a people\u2019s lords before a sorcerer comes a-conquering, or to act as a signaller ahead of invasion to hidden elements of rebellion. These things they do without complaint, so long as their price is right, for their mentality is mercenary. In payment, they ask all manner of things - that the name of a firstborn child be this rather than that, favours to be named in future, or that they be given the pick of three men from a sorcerer\u2019s holdings to go with them, wherever they take them.<br /> <br /> Often, these prices seem little enough to such great men at first, but many years later have unforeseen effects. Sacrifices long-presumed dead will return with new and dark learning to challenge their former masters, demon-chosen names will incite the hatred of those who might have been allies, and favours that seemed light at first become chains later on. Some perceive a deeper meaning in these turns of chance than the disasters and calamities loved by the children of the Ultimate Darkness, and even whisper that Buha has a standing arrangement with the viziers of Fate, acting to further the plans of destiny in some hidden way. But what agents of Heaven would consort with such a blood-drinking creature of night? Such is always a part of the President\u2019s retainer.<br /> <br /> Buha may slip the bonds of Hell when an owl or other night-bird drinks the blood of a young man and a suckling lamb in a single night; that bird becomes one of their many bodies, and flies out to bring more through to Creation. They gain Limit when their prices are denied or cheated after having been promised, and will exact terrible revenges upon such as do so - though they may be long in coming.<br /> <br /> <b>Tanlato, the Inquisitor Circumspect</b><br /> <i>Demon of the Second Circle<br /> Warden Soul of the House of the Scorpion</i><br /> <br /> Two heads has Tanlato, the Heron Who Eats Dreams. That is a name he buries deep, though, and there are few who know it. He has two forms as well. One is a man of saturnine aspect, tall and dark-haired, with the severely-carven features of a man of the Blessed Isle and the blood of Danada, but with doubled pupils in each eye and teeth of hard metal. The other is a two-headed heron whose height can vary from reaching a tall man\u2019s knee to towering several feet above him, and whose beaks are made of steel. In either form he goes clad in black and red, whether these be his feathers or his robes, and he may be known by the clack of his talons upon the earth.<br /> <br /> In demeanour the Inquisitor Circumspect is reserved but keen of wit, rarely failing to offer a cutting remark when he perceives some failing he can criticise - and he sees many, for his eyes are just as keen. Often he resides within his greater self, acting to police and regulate the many students of Dascal - but he may also go abroad, leaving his demons to do so in his stead. For this he is little-loved by those students, but it has long since taught him how to keep order even amongst the rowdiest and most unmanageable populations, and has become a masterful driver of slaves and servants of all kinds. His eyes can perceive hatred and resentment as easily as another might note the colour of a man\u2019s hair, and with attention and time can discern particulars such as against whom that resentment is directed.<br /> <br /> His most significant ability, though, is known to few - and Tanlato puts great effort to keeping it this way. His beaks have the power to plunge into the head of another, and there his sensitive tongues can taste the memories of his victims. With the right head he picks out memories of events and places, and with the left he devours abstract knowledge. Thus it is that few students go forth from the House of the Scorpion with any knowledge of where to find it again, and Dascal is protected from the dangers of his great vice. The Inquisitor has served this office since his creation, but some say that he has become bitter with the years, and does so now out of a sense of obligation, habit and the fear of what might befall his oversoul - and thus himself - were the House left without his guardianship.<br /> <br /> <i>Summoning (Obscurity 3/6):</i> Demonologists summon the Inquisitor Circumspect to put down rebellions and command unruly servants, to pick out spies and rebels amongst their followers, and for his knowledge and might as a sorcerer. In this he is as practical as his sister Alean is abstract, and knows many spells for confinement, death and the warding-away of hostile powers and attention. Those who know of Tanlato\u2019s other talent, however, summon him to be a censor and interrogator, for in the taste of the memories he swallows he can glean much from victims\u2019 minds - and what he cannot take by magic, he can take by torment, as he has had long practice in the art of interrogation.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, he is a master of the Black Heron Style, a discipline of his own invention and an offshoot of Crane Style. This Style focuses on non-fatal defence and subduing attacks in a manner similar to its origin, but where Crane Style relies upon enlightened discourse to educate and edify its target, the Black Heron Style instead uses a combination of force and humiliation to subdue the target to its practitioner\u2019s will through fear and coercion. Although known in Creation, it is poorly-regarded as unsportsmanlike and reviled as a dark mirror of the Crane.<br /> <br /> Some say the Inquisitor\u2019s role as a censor has brought him into some alignment with the End of All Wisdom, the ancient enemy of Dascal, and that he has some plot to muzzle, or perhaps somehow even overthrow and replace his greater self in the ranks of the Unquestionable. If such a thing is possible, perhaps Dascal would marvel at the beauty of his own destruction in the moment of betrayal. Tanlato gains Limit when one he had thought broken defies him, and may escape into Creation when the head of a monastery or formal school is imprisoned by rebellious students and begs for anyone to deliver him and restore the right order of the world. Then the Inquisitor will appear and with hands and beaks and sorcery set things to rights for that school, before departing on errands of his own - but who can tell, after he has come, whether all is as it once was or what he has taken?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}